  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "In all of the following, $E$ stands for the universal set.\n\nState whether each statement is true or false. Explain your answers.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(A^c)^c=A$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True; “not not in $A$” means “in $A$”.",
          "worked": "The complement of $A^c$ contains exactly the elements of $E$ that are not outside $A$. These are the elements of $A$, so $(A^c)^c=A$. The statement is true.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$A\\cup A^c=E$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True; every element of $E$ is either in $A$ or in $A^c$.",
          "worked": "Every element of $E$ is either in $A$ or not in $A$. The latter elements form $A^c$, so their union contains all of $E$. Thus $A\\cup A^c=E$, and the statement is true.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$A\\cap A^c=E$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False; $A\\cap A^c=\\varnothing$.",
          "worked": "No element can be both in $A$ and not in $A$. Therefore $A$ and $A^c$ have no elements in common: $A\\cap A^c=\\varnothing$. The statement is false.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$E^c=E$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False; $E^c=\\varnothing$.",
          "worked": "The complement is taken within $E$. There are no elements of $E$ outside $E$, so $E^c=\\varnothing$. The statement is false.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\varnothing^c=E$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True; every element of $E$ is outside the empty set.",
          "worked": "The empty set contains no elements. Consequently every element of $E$ belongs to its complement, so $\\varnothing^c=E$. The statement is true.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$|A|=|A^c|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. For example, if $E=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $A=\\{1\\}$, then $|A|=1$ and $|A^c|=2$.",
          "worked": "Take $E=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $A=\\{1\\}$. Then $A^c=\\{2,3\\}$, so $|A|=1$ and $|A^c|=2$. These cardinalities differ, providing a counterexample. The statement is false.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
